## 🧩 Detailed Component Breakdown

### 1. Frontend (Cost: **₹0/month**)

| Choice | Why |
|---|---|
| **Next.js 15 (App Router)** | SSR + SSG for fast loads, great SEO |
| **Hosted on Vercel** | Free tier: 100GB bandwidth, serverless functions |
| **PWA** | Offline support, installable, push notifications |
| **Framer Motion** | Duolingo-style micro-animations |

**Gamification UI Components:**
- 🔥 Streak counter with animated fire icon
- ⭐ XP bar with level progression
- 🏆 Weekly leaderboards with leagues (Bronze → Diamond)
- 🎖️ Achievement badges with unlock animations
- 💚 Mascot character (like Duo owl) for encouragement
- 📊 Performance radar charts per subject

---

### 2. Authentication (Cost: **₹0/month**)

| Choice | Why |
|---|---|
| **Supabase Auth** | 50,000 MAU free, OAuth, Magic Link, Phone OTP |
| **Social Logins** | Google, Apple — most school kids have Google |

---

### 3. Backend / API Layer (Cost: **₹0–500/month**)

> [!TIP]
> Avoid running a 24/7 server at all costs. Use **serverless functions** that scale to zero.

**Option A: Supabase Edge Functions (Recommended for MVP)**
- 500K invocations/month FREE
- Runs on Deno — fast cold starts
- Direct access to Supabase DB

**Option B: Cloudflare Workers (for heavy traffic)**
- 100K requests/day FREE
- Global edge deployment — ultra-low latency
- Workers AI for running open-source models at the edge

**API Design:**
```
POST /api/exam/generate      → AI generates exam questions
POST /api/exam/submit         → Submit answers, get score
GET  /api/exam/history        → Past exam results
GET  /api/recommend           → AI recommendations based on scores
POST /api/prep/material       → AI generates study material
GET  /api/user/stats          → XP, streak, level, badges
GET  /api/leaderboard         → Weekly leaderboard
POST /api/doubt/ask           → RAG-powered doubt solving
```

---

### 4. Database (Cost: **₹0/month**)

**Supabase PostgreSQL (Free Tier: 500MB, 2 projects)**

```sql
-- Core Tables
users (id, name, email, avatar, grade, board, xp, level, streak, created_at)
subjects (id, name, grade, board)
topics (id, subject_id, name, chapter_no)
exams (id, user_id, subject_id, topic_id, score, total, created_at)
exam_questions (id, exam_id, question, options, correct_answer, user_answer, is_correct)
study_materials (id, topic_id, content_type, content, ai_generated)
user_badges (id, user_id, badge_type, earned_at)
user_streaks (id, user_id, date, completed)

-- Caching Layer
question_cache (id, topic_id, difficulty, questions_json, created_at, ttl)
```

**Upstash Redis (Free: 10K commands/day)**
- Cache leaderboard rankings
- Cache AI responses for common questions
- Rate limiting per user

---

### 5. AI Engine — The Brain (Cost: **₹500–2000/month**)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is the only component that costs real money. The strategy: **cache aggressively + use cheapest models.**

#### LLM Strategy (Tiered)

| Tier | Model | Cost | Use Case |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Free** | Gemini 2.0 Flash (Free tier) | ₹0 | Question generation, study material |
| **Cheap** | DeepSeek V3 API | ~$0.07/1M input tokens | Complex reasoning, doubt solving |
| **Fallback** | Groq + Llama 3.3 | Free tier available | Backup when rate-limited |

#### RAG Implementation (Cost: **₹0** with Supabase)

```mermaid
graph LR
    A[NCERT/Textbook PDFs] --> B[Chunk & Embed<br/>text-embedding-004]
    B --> C[Supabase pgvector<br/>Vector Store]
    D[Student Question] --> E[Embed Query]
    E --> F[Similarity Search<br/>pgvector]
    F --> G[Top-K Context Chunks]
    G --> H[LLM + Context<br/>= Accurate Answer]
```

**RAG Data Sources:**
- NCERT textbooks (Class 6–12) — public domain
- State board syllabus documents
- Previous year question papers
- Teacher-curated notes (community)

**Embedding Model:** Google `text-embedding-004` (Free tier: 1,500 requests/min)

**Vector Store:** Supabase `pgvector` extension — **completely free** with your existing Supabase DB.

#### Cost Optimization Tricks:
1. **Pre-generate & cache** question banks per topic/difficulty — don't call LLM every time
2. **Batch process** study material during off-peak (night cron jobs)
3. **Template-based generation** — LLM fills in variables, not generates from scratch
4. **Token limit discipline** — max 500 input + 1000 output tokens per call
5. **Deduplication** — hash questions to avoid regenerating identical ones

---

